      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-esc">Escalation path (30%):</strong> Both the October 14 session (<span style="color:var(--accent);font-family:monospace;font-size:0.9em;">F2</span>) and the year-end framework (<span style="color:var(--accent);font-family:monospace;font-size:0.9em;">F4</span>) fail; talks collapse and fighting resumes at or above September scale. Derivation: (1−0.60)×(1−0.22) ≈ 31%, rounded to 30%.</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-prot">Protracted path (45%):</strong> Mediation continues across Oman, Qatar, and US channels without producing a binding framework; Hormuz stays below 30 vessels per day through year-end; stalemate persists into 2027.</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-desc">De-escalation path (25%):</strong> The ceasefire framework (<span style="color:var(--accent);font-family:monospace;font-size:0.9em;">F4</span>) is reached, or the October session (<span style="color:var(--accent);font-family:monospace;font-size:0.9em;">F2</span>) advances sufficiently to produce an early framework before December 31. Derivation: p(F4)=0.22 + marginal F2-to-framework credit ≈ 0.25.</p>
    </div>
